No, I don't mean really stale tins, I mean tins like Hack 1.0.1 had. 
Back then tins didn't have monsters in them just certain pre-set contents.

One was spinanch, which is still around, there others were:
* It contains first quality peaches - what a surprise!
IIRC these would sometimes confuse you, presumably because they were 
brandied.

* It contains salmon - not bad!
The ancescter of deep fried tins. (Slippery fingers.)

*It contains apple juice - perhaps not what you hoped for.
This would be <fruit> juice now, of course.

*It contains some nondescript substance, tasting awfully.
But it actually had decent food value.

*It contains rotten meat. You vomit.
Just generic "meat" but otherwise the same as curently.

*It turns out to be empty.
This still happens in some situations too, I guess.

So three of those are unlike anything in tcurrent versions of Nethack: 
peaches, juice and "nondescript substance". It just struck me the other 
day that it would be fun to see those make a comeback, possibly along 
with a few new ones.

